  {
    "id" : "DL3049",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Enforce Required Label Presence",
    "description" : "This rule ensures that all labels specified by a label-schema are present in the Dockerfile.",
    "explanation" : "## Label `<label>` is missing\n\nThis rule is only activated, when specifying a label-schema. The examples used on this wiki page presume the label-schema is:\n```yaml\nlabel-schema:\n  version: text\n```\nor specified via command line:\n```bash\n$ hadolint --require-label version\n```\n\n### Problematic code example:\n```Dockerfile\nFROM busybox\n```\n\n### Correct code example:\n```Dockerfile\nFROM busybox\nLABEL version=\"1.0.1\"\n```\n\n### Rationale:\nWhen a label-schema is specified, all labels within that schema must be present.",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "DL3050",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "BestPractice",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Superfluous Labels in Dockerfile",
    "description" : "Detects and disallows superfluous labels in Dockerfiles when using strict label enforcement.",
    "explanation" : "## Superfluous label(s) present.\n\nThis rule is only activated when linting with the `strict-labels` option. This can be specified via config file\n```yaml\nstrict-labels: true\n```\nor via command line:\n```bash\n$ hadolint --strict-labels Dockerfile\n```\nNote, that when no label-schema is specified, all labels are considered superfluous by this rule.\n\n### Problematic code:\n```Dockerfile\nFROM busybox\nLABEL superfluous=\"this should not be here\"\n```\n\n### Correct code:\n```Dockerfile\nFROM busybox\n```\n\n### Rationale:\nIn certain situations, it may be desirable to ensure no labels other than those specified in the label-schema are present. This may be required to avoid information leakage, to not confuse label parsers or to ensure compliance to standards.",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 5,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
    ]
  },
  {
    "id" : "DL3051",
    "level" : "Warning",
    "category" : "ErrorProne",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Avoid Empty Labels in Dockerfile",
    "description" : "This rule checks that labels in Dockerfiles are not empty when required by the label-schema.",
    "explanation" : "## Label `<label>` is empty.\n\nThis rule is activated by specifying a label-schema.\n\n### Problematic code:\n```Dockerfile\nLABEL oopsie=\"\"\n```\n\n### Correct code:\n```Dockerfile\nLABEL oopsie=\"whoopsie\"\n```\n\n### Rationale\nWhen a label is required by the specified label-schema, it should not be empty or else there would be no sense in requiring the label in the first place.",
    "enabled" : false,
    "timeToFix" : 3,
    "parameters" : [
    ],
    "languages" : [
